{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297364-tables-to-randomize-instruments-for-magickal-effects","id":1297364,"title":"Tables to randomize instruments for magickal effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-16T15:12:32-07:00","id":1297364,"title":"Tables to randomize instruments for magickal effects","content":"Some players tend to hand-wave or outright &quot;forget&quot; magickal instruments (a.k.a. foci) when casting an effect.<br /> I've found this might be because<br /> * they've either been using the same rote/Sphere multiple times over the session or the campaign, and the &quot;same instrument/focus for same effect&quot; and the &quot;same instrument for same Sphere&quot; has got boring;<br /> * or they've got tired of coming up with novel practices that still conform to their paradigm.<br /> (It might also be a failing on my part as storyteller, but let's not go there right now<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A solution that seems to work is having a table with instruments numbered 1-10 for each of the players (who want one - no pressure), personalized for their paradigm and practices.<br /> When casting an effect, the player rolls d10 and gets a &quot;random&quot; instrument for that particular effect. They might have that instrument available just there and then, in which case it's cool, or they might not, in which case better luck next time.<br /> The instruments need to be generally worded so that they could be used in a variety of situations.<br /> Instrument tables can have sub-tables if the instruments can be grouped into categories - the player rolls on the &quot;master&quot; table, and if they roll a number that corresponds to a sub-table, they roll again.<br /> Every few sessions or so you and your player should mix it up a little, bring in new items, lose ones that got old, to prevent getting into a rut.<br /> <br /> This does not affect rotes with fixed instruments.<br /> Example: I have a gnostic Russian Orthodox-type demon hunter inspired by equal parts Rasputin and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HedfBEukl4c\" target=\"_blank\">Werner Herzog's Bells from the Deep</a>. His current instruments master table is<br /> 1 - Kiss the Christ Pantocrator icon around your neck;<br /> 2 - Let loose your booming voice<br /> 3 - Laying on of hands.<br /> 4 - Ecstatic singing.<br /> 5 - Mortification of the flesh, see sub-table 1<br /> 6 - Cross yourself the Orthodox way<br /> 7 - Pray/knead/finger the rosary<br /> 8 - Show subject the crucifix<br /> 9 - Bless or curse, see sub-table 2<br /> 10 - Open Bible at random, read first passage<br /> <br /> Sub-table 1<br /> 1 - Self-flagellation<br /> 2 - 4 Fasting (the effect will only be successful if the caster has been fasting for at least 12 hours)<br /> 5 - 7 Repeated prostration<br /> 8 -10 Beat yourself on chest at least 3 times<br /> <br /> Sub-table 2<br /> 1-3 Support blessing/curse with consecrated ointment.<br /> 4 - 6 Support blessing/curse with rose water.<br /> 7 - 10 Support blessing/curse with ritual incense<br /> <br /> What do you think? Is this something some sourcebook has mentioned? Is anyone doing anything similar? Is it silly? Is there a better way to achieve the same thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://budapest-urban-fantasy.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Write-up for an alternate history Mage: The Ascension setting</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24482-aproragadozo","name":"aproragadozo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24482_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T01:37:13-07:00","id":1297658,"title":"","content":"Mmmh, I'm not sure how I'd feel about having a random instrument forced upon me when trying to cast an effect. It does not really make sense to me - why being forced to use an instrument you might not be carrying with you, when it's been proven that the very same effect can be cast with an instrument you actually happen to be carrying around with you at the time? Also, not every type of instrument is even suited for a specific situation. I'll get to that below.<br /> <br /> Personally I think one of the best changes of M20 was the breakaway from the direct tie of &quot;this instrument for this sphere&quot;. It never made sense to me due to the vastly different kinds of effects one can do with a single sphere.<br /> Not that there also is no rule of &quot;Only one instrument for a specific effect&quot;! The fact that you can freely pick from several of your chosen instruments for a specific effect in M20 is great, allowing for flexibility as long as the instrument is picked from the ones you decided on in character generation, and it makes sense for the effect in question.<br /> And while not every instrument makes sense for every effect, it just feels organic and &quot;realistic&quot; to have a certain subset of your instruments available for a certain kind of magick.<br /> <br /> What you could encourage your players to do is, to switch it up depending on the situation - some instruments are good for fast-casting, some are better suited for rituals. Even if they are used for the same type of effect.<br /> In your example above, the crucifix would be ideal for a short combat-round Ward or Ban to push back an enemy - but to establish a long-term ward, a ritual of ecstatic singing might be the thing to go for. Things like that. Players should have *fun* trying to flesh out just how their character does certain things, and this kind of instrument flexibility helps with that.<br /> <br /> Also note that if your players are Arete 3 or higher, you can take notes of what instruments they use for what, and which instruments seem to be the least important ones...and then work the &quot;dropping of instruments&quot; rule into their RP; A character suddenly realizing they didn't use one of their lesser instruments in a short fast-casting, and from then on not needing an instrument for that effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-18-2019, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T04:05:40-07:00","id":1297683,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297364-tables-to-randomize-instruments-for-magickal-effects?p=1297658#post1297658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmh, I'm not sure how I'd feel about having a random instrument forced upon me when trying to cast an effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you put it like that, it does sound constraining<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> This could work for a &quot;chaos&quot; mage espousing &quot;Crazy Wisdom&quot; as a practice with a matching paradigm (something like <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dice_Man\" target=\"_blank\">the Dice Man</a>, perhaps?), but you're right: most mages are more rigorous and/or more &quot;scientific&quot; in their magickal approach to have a random table tell them about instruments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297364-tables-to-randomize-instruments-for-magickal-effects?p=1297658#post1297658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not every type of instrument is even suited for a specific situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think this is a plus - having a fixed, not necessarily well-suited instrument for an effect promotes creative thinking on the player's part - though this might bring about unintentional comedy.<br /> <br /> The idea of explicitly curating a set of instruments, some of which are &quot;core&quot; or &quot;primary&quot; for certain Spheres/effects to identify the &quot;peripheral&quot; or &quot;secondary&quot; instruments that could be dropped later on is also nice. However, I think random instrument tables aren't incompatible with this - The set of instruments that the player fleshes out for themselves could then be put into such a table, and then, once an instrument is dropped, that given row in the table is blanked out, so that next time that option is rolled on the table, the player does not need any instrument for the effect.<br /> <br /> Overall, though, I agree that this idea definitely needs more thought, and random instrument tables should only be used for mages with a compatible paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://budapest-urban-fantasy.blogspot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Write-up for an alternate history Mage: The Ascension setting</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24482-aproragadozo","name":"aproragadozo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24482_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}